{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>You prepare</b> — against my enemies: corresponding to 'in the valley of the shadow of death,' in the manner of 'from the sight of distress.'" "<b>And behold, the table</b> — corresponding to 'the grass.'" "<b>And my cup is saturated</b> — corresponding to 'upon still waters.'" "<b>Saturated</b> — a predicate of HaShem, like 'a wise woman' and 'rich in fatness'; the delicacies that are upon the table — its head is fattened, as though it is mixed with fresh oil. And the meaning of this psalm is concerning the servants of HaShem who abandon the desires of the world and are joyful in their portion, and they reckon that bread and water correspond to every delight of delicacies, for their thought and heart are upon the delights of the world to come; therefore they leave the pleasure of a moment for the pleasure of eternity. Therefore he said: 'only this is all my thought,' and 'let them pursue me' — so much will I accustom myself to do good and kindness."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {3 "'אשה חכמה' and 'מרוב דשן' appear to be understood as predicate constructions serving as grammatical parallels to רויה; 'ראשו מדושן' is rendered hyper-literally as 'its head is fattened' — the construction is strained and may reflect textual difficulty."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:26.198245559Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}